   "daf": "10a",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ בֵּית שַׁמַּאי אוֹמְרִים: לֹא יִטּוֹל אֶלָּא אִם כֵּן נִעְנַע מִבְּעוֹד יוֹם. וּבֵית הִלֵּל אוֹמְרִים: עוֹמֵד וְאוֹמֵר ״זֶה וָזֶה אֲנִי נוֹטֵל״.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «Beit Shammai say: One may not take» fledgling doves from a dovecote on a Festival, «unless he shook» the ones he wished to take «while it was still day,» thereby preparing them. «And Beit Hillel say:» It is not necessary to shake; rather, it is sufficient if one «stands» the day before «and says: I» will «take this» fledgling «and that» one."
  }
 ],
